  "job_B1.3.5_20251001_193222": {
    "text": "IDVS IANVARII.\nPASSIO SANCTI IVLIANI ET SPONSE EIVS BASILISSE.\nIVLIANVS W\u00e6S GEHATEN SUM \u00c6\u00d0ELE GODES \u00f0EGN ON Egypta lande, on antiochian \u00fe\u00e6re\n\u00dea wolde his f\u00e6der and his frynd ealle \u00fe\u00e6t he wifian sceolde \u00fea \u00f0e he eahtetyne g\u00e6ra w\u00e6s, ac Iulianus\nHe wear\u00f0 \u00fea gebysgod on his gebedum seofan niht, b\u00e6d \u00feone \u00e6lmihtigan Crist \u00fe\u00e6t he his cl\u00e6nnysse\n\u00d0a \u00e6teowde se h\u00e6lend hine sylfne on swefne \u00feam \u00e6\u00feelan cnihte on \u00f0\u00e6re eahteo\u00f0an nihte, and cw\u00e6\u00f0\nSe H\u00e6lend him cw\u00e6\u00f0 to, Ic beo sylf mid \u00fee, and on \u00fee adwesce ealle ontendnysse, and \u00fe\u00e6t m\u00e6den ic\n\u00d0a awoc Iulianus gewyssod \u00feurh his drihten, cw\u00e6\u00f0 to his freondum \u00fe\u00e6t he onfon wolde m\u00e6den him to\n\u00dea fundon his magas sum \u00e6\u00f0elboren m\u00e6den Basilissa gehaten, and him \u00fea begeaten.\n\u00dea wurdon gegearcode \u00fea gyftu \u00e6fter gewunan, and hi butu coman on anum bedde tosomne.\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a Iulianus hine georne geb\u00e6d to \u00f0am h\u00e6lende Criste, \u00fe\u00e6t he hine geheolde wi\u00f0 ealla\n\u00d0a wear\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t brydbed mid br\u00e6\u00f0e afylled swylce \u00fe\u00e6r l\u00e6gon lilie and rose.\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 Basilissa to \u00feam cl\u00e6nan brydguman, Hit is wintertid nu and ic wundrie \u00feearle hwanon \u00fees\nIulianus andwyrde \u00feam \u00e6\u00f0elan m\u00e6dene, \u00fees wynsuman br\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fee \u00f0u wundrast \u00feearle n\u00e6f\u00f0 nan angin ne\n\u00dees br\u00e6\u00f0 is of Criste se\u00f0e is cl\u00e6nnysse lufigend, gif wit \u00feurhwunia\u00f0 on ansundum m\u00e6g\u00f0hade, and hine\nBasilissa cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t heo on cl\u00e6num m\u00e6g\u00f0hade \u00feurhwunian wolde for \u00f0am wynsuman behate, and\n\u00dea clypode Iulianus on cneowgebedum \u00f0us, Confirma hoc deus, quod operatus es in nobis et reliqua.\nGef\u00e6stna \u00feis H\u00e6lend, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u on us gewyrcst.\nAnd Basilissa sona swa gelice dyde.\n\u00dea astyrede \u00fe\u00e6t brydbed and beorht leoht \u00fe\u00e6r scean.\nAnd Crist wear\u00f0 gesewen mid scinendum werode, and his modur Maria mid hyre m\u00e6denlicum heape.\nCrist clypode \u00fea to \u00f0am cl\u00e6nan cnihte, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he h\u00e6fde oferswi\u00f0od woruldlice g\u00e6lsan and \u00feone\nOf Marian werode w\u00e6s \u00feus geclypod, Eadig eart \u00feu Basilissa, for\u00fean \u00fee \u00feu gebygdest \u00fein mod to\n\u00dea com to \u00f0am bedde boc fram \u00feam H\u00e6lende.\nAnd twegen his halgan mid twam cynehelmum ar\u00e6rdan hi \u00fea upp and heton hi r\u00e6dan.\n\u00d0a r\u00e6dde Iulianus \u00feas word on \u00fe\u00e6re bec, Se \u00fee for minre lufe middaneard forsih\u00f0, he bi\u00f0 so\u00f0lice\nBasilissa bi\u00f0 geteald to \u00fe\u00e6ra m\u00e6dena get\u00e6le \u00fee Marian folgia\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6s h\u00e6lendes meder.\n\u00c6fter \u00feissere r\u00e6dinge and o\u00f0rum tihtingum gewendon \u00fea halgan to \u00feam H\u00e6lende upp.\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea Iulianus ungew\u00e6mmede heold his bryde, and hi w\u00e6ron ge\u00f0eodde mid so\u00f0re cl\u00e6nnysse\nHeora f\u00e6deras w\u00e6ron gefyrn cristene; hit gelamp \u00fea ra\u00f0e \u00fe\u00e6t hi of life gewytan, and l\u00e6fdon heora \u00e6hta\nIulianus \u00fea d\u00e6lde be his drihtnes wyssunga heora land are \u00fee him l\u00e6fed w\u00e6s, and ar\u00e6rde him mynster\nHe wear\u00f0 \u00fea f\u00e6der ofer f\u00e6la muneca, and Basilissa modor ofer manega mynecena; and hi \u00fea gastlican\n\u00dea geb\u00e6don \u00fea halgan hi to \u00feam h\u00e6lende.\nAnd he him asende \u00feisne frofer \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00f0ende, Eala \u00feu Basilissa \u00feine gebedu synd gefyllede \u00fe\u00e6t ealle\nHit wear\u00f0 \u00fea gefylled, swa swa him fores\u00e6de God, \u00fe\u00e6t ealle \u00f0a femnan \u00fee folgodon Basilissan\nAnd Basilissa si\u00f0\u00f0an so\u00f0lice gela\u00f0od gewat on m\u00e6g\u00f0hade of middanearde to Criste.\nAnd Iulianus mid blisse hi bebyrgde mid his munecum; And he abad on life mid his leofan gebro\u00f0rum\n\u00d0a com Martianus se manfulla cw\u00e6llere into Antiochian \u00fe\u00e6re Egyptiscan byrig mid ormettre ehtnysse\nHe sette \u00f0a gebann \u00fe\u00e6t nan mann bicgan ne moste o\u00f0\u00f0e \u00e6nig \u00feing syllan buton he ons\u00e6gednysse\nHim wear\u00f0 \u00fea ges\u00e6d be \u00f0am so\u00f0an geleafan \u00fee Iulianus heold mid his halgum gebro\u00f0rum, and sende\nAc Iulianus ne rohte \u00fe\u00e6s re\u00f0an \u00feywrace, ne nan his geferena forht n\u00e6s on mode, ac w\u00e6ron lustb\u00e6re\n\u00dea gecyrde se \u00e6rendraca and \u00feis s\u00e6de \u00feam deman.\nMartianus \u00fea het \u00feone halgan Iulianum him to gelangian to langsumum wytum, and het si\u00f0\u00f0an\n\u00dea wear\u00f0 se halga heap \u00feam h\u00e6lende geoffrod, and \u00feurh \u00fe\u00e6t hate fyr to heofonan rice becom.\nOn \u00f0ere stowe beo\u00f0 geh\u00e6lede gehwilce untrume \u00feurh \u00fe\u00e6ra martyra geearnunga \u00fee on \u00fe\u00e6re stowe\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a Martianus se manfulla cwellere h\u00e6fde langsum gewinn wi\u00f0 \u00feone \u00e6\u00f0elan Iulianum, and\nAnd ic \u00fee for\u00f0i tihte \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u \u00feam godum geoffrige \u00e6fter \u00feinre gebyrde, \u00fe\u00e6t hi \u00fee bly\u00f0e beon.\nIulianus him s\u00e6de, \u00feu eart so\u00f0lice ablend mid \u00feinre yfelnysse and for\u00fei me \u00feus ol\u00e6cst.\nGe habba\u00f0 manega godas and manega gydena, we so\u00f0lice wur\u00f0ian \u00e6nne so\u00f0ne god.\nEower godas synd agotene o\u00f0\u00f0e agrafene, hu magon hi beon gegladode \u00feurh \u00e6nige bigencgas o\u00fe\u00fee\n\u00deeos race is swi\u00f0e langsum fullice to gereccenne, ac we hit s\u00e6cga\u00f0 eow on \u00fea scortostan wisan.\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea Martianus het his manfullan cwelleras \u00feone halgan beatan mid heardum saglum.\n\u00dea b\u00e6rst sum sagol into anes beateres eagan, swa \u00fe\u00e6t his eage wand ut mid \u00feam sl\u00e6ge.\nSe man w\u00e6s \u00feam deman \u00feearle nydbehefe and cu\u00f0 \u00feam casere and him eallum gecweme.\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 Martianus mid mycclum graman, swa micel is \u00fein drycr\u00e6ft \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u \u00feas dyntas naht ne\nIulianus \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0 to \u00feam welhreowan \u00feus, Clypia\u00f0 to eowrum godum and to eallum gydenum \u00fe\u00e6t hi\n\u00dea eoden \u00fea h\u00e6\u00f0engyldan into heora temple, clypigende hlude to \u00f0am leasan gode.\n\u00d0a andwerdan \u00fea deofla of \u00feam d\u00e6dan anlicnyssum, Gewita\u00f0 fram us we synd wra\u00f0e gesw\u00e6ncte and\nHu mage we blinde \u00feone blindan geh\u00e6lan?\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Iulianus \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6t eal wyste to Martiane mid micelre blisse, Gang into \u00feinum godum \u00fee hi\n\u00dea eode se ehtere into \u00f0am temple, and geseah \u00fea anlicnyssa ealle tocwysede gyldena and sylfrena and\n\u00dea s\u00e6de Martianus \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0a so\u00f0f\u00e6stan godes mid ge\u00feylde forb\u00e6ron \u00feone bysmorfullan teonan, \u00fe\u00e6t hi\nHe b\u00e6d swa \u00feeah Iulianum \u00fe\u00e6t he his gebeot gel\u00e6ste, and \u00fe\u00e6s cnihtes eage \u00feurh his Crist geh\u00e6lde.\n\u00dea m\u00e6rcode Iulianus \u00fe\u00e6s mannes eage mid Cristes rodetacne and se cniht wear\u00f0 geh\u00e6led, swylce his\n\u00d0a clypode se cniht and cw\u00e6\u00f0 to Martiane, Se god is to gelyfanne \u00fee \u00f0a Cristenan ongelyfa\u00f0, and \u00feine\nMartianus \u00fea het hine beheafdian for\u00f0an \u00fee he gelyfde on \u00feone lyfigendan God \u00fee his eage onlihte\nHe het eac geswencean mid swarum witum \u00feone halgan Iulianum, and het hine l\u00e6dan geond ealle \u00fea\nMartianus h\u00e6fde his sunu \u00e6r bef\u00e6st to woruldlicre lare and to u\u00f0witegunge, on \u00fe\u00e6re ylcan byrig \u00fee se\nHis nama w\u00e6s Celsus and se geseah \u00feone halgan, and hu godes \u00e6nglas him mid flugon.\nAwearp \u00fea his larboc and mid geleafan arn to \u00feam halgan were and his fet gesohte, cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he\nNe mihte hine nan man of \u00feam geleafan gebringan, ne fram Iuliane \u00feurh \u00e6nig \u00feing ateon.\n\u00dea w\u00e6r\u00f0 Martianus and eac seo modor dreorige on mode, and heora men ealle.\nAnd Martianus befran \u00feone m\u00e6ran Iulianum, hwi woldest \u00feu amyrran min ancennedan sunu \u00feurh\nBeheald ure sarnysse and urne sunu forl\u00e6t, and ic \u00f0e ge\u00feingie to urum kasere.\nCelsus se sunu s\u00e6de \u00feam swicolan f\u00e6der \u00feus, Ic wi\u00f0sace \u00fee f\u00e6der for \u00feinum gedwylde, and ic gelyfa\nWitna gif \u00feu wylle mid w\u00e6lhreowum tintregum \u00feinne agenre sunu for \u00feinra goda bigencge.\nGif \u00feu nelle me ofslean, asend me to \u00feam casere, \u00fe\u00e6t ic \u00fe\u00e6r dea\u00f0 \u00ferowige for minum drihtne Criste.\n\u00dea halgan wurdon gebrohte on blindum cwearterne sy\u00f0\u00f0an be Martianes h\u00e6se \u00fe\u00e6r manna lic lagon, \u00fee\n\u00dea foresceawode Godes gifu \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r scean mycel leoht and se stenc wear\u00f0 awend to wynsumum\n\u00dea cw\u00e6don \u00fea cempan \u00fee se cwellere gesette \u00feam halgum to weardmannum, \u00fe\u00e6ra w\u00e6ron twentig,\nHi feollon \u00fea ealle to Iulianes fotum, mid geleafan herigende \u00fe\u00e6s H\u00e6lendes naman.\nIulianus \u00fea b\u00e6d mid onbryrdnysse his drihten, \u00fe\u00e6t he foresceawode hu hi gefullode wurdon.\n\u00de\u00e6r w\u00e6ron binnan \u00fe\u00e6re byrig seofan gebro\u00f0ra Cristena, \u00fe\u00e6s caseres cynnes, and heora f\u00e6der w\u00e6s\nHi h\u00e6fdon \u00e6nne m\u00e6ssepreost swi\u00f0e m\u00e6res lifes, Antonius gehaten, \u00fee him m\u00e6ssan gesang.\n\u00deas geneosode se H\u00e6lend, and het hi gan to \u00feam cwearterne mid heora m\u00e6ssepreoste, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fea men\nHi eoden \u00fea on niht and Godes \u00e6ngel hi l\u00e6dde and \u00fe\u00e6t cweartern geopenade mid his handa hrepunge.\n\u00dea s\u00e6don \u00fea gebro\u00f0ra \u00fe\u00e6t se h\u00e6lend hi asende mid heora m\u00e6ssepreost\u00e6 \u00fea men to fullienne.\nIulianus \u00fea sona \u00fe\u00e6s \u00feancode Gode, and wear\u00f0 \u00fea gefullod se fores\u00e6da cnapa, and his f\u00e6der cempan\n\u00deis w\u00e6ar\u00f0 \u00fea gecyd \u00feam cwellere Martiane, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fea seofan gebro\u00f0ra butan \u00e6lcere ehtnysse woldan for\n\u00dea het se cwellere hi of \u00feam cwearterne gel\u00e6dan, and axode hwi hi woldan butan ehtnysse \u00ferowian.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se yldesta bro\u00f0or to \u00feam arleasan deman, Ands\u00e6te bi\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t treow \u00fee \u00e6fre grew\u00f0 on leafum\n\u00dea het se cwellere hi to \u00feam cwearterne gel\u00e6dan, and sende his gewrit to \u00feam w\u00e6lhreowan casere,\n\u00dea asende se casere \u00feisne cwide ongean, gif Iulianus \u00feurhwuna\u00f0 mid his geferum on \u00feysum, nim fela\nAnd gif he \u00feurh his drycr\u00e6ft \u00fe\u00e6t fyr adwescan m\u00e6g, gewitna hi ealle loca hu \u00feu wylle.\n\u00dea het Martianus \u00fea godes menn gefeccan, and axode Iulianum hwe\u00f0er hi aht smeadon ymbe hyre\nIulianus s\u00e6de, ure ge\u00feanc is swa swa hit w\u00e6s; gif \u00feu \u00e6nig wite be\u00feohtest, we synd gearwe to \u00feam.\n\u00dea mid \u00feyssere spr\u00e6ce b\u00e6ron menn on \u00f0\u00e6re str\u00e6t anes h\u00e6\u00f0enes mannes lic, and se heardheorta dema\nCw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fea to Iuliane, Eower Crist ar\u00e6rde \u00fea deadan to life, l\u00e6t nu geswutelian gif he so\u00f0 God sy, and\n\u00dea andwyrde iulianus \u00feam arleasan deman, Hw\u00e6t frema\u00f0 \u00feam blindan seo beorhta sunbeam?\nIs swa \u00feeah tima \u00fe\u00e6t Godes miht beo geswutelod.\nIulianus \u00f0a hof to heofonum his eagan, biddende his drihten \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00feone deadan ar\u00e6rde.\n\u00dea \u00e6fter anre tida aras se deade and clypode ofer eall, Eala hu andf\u00e6ncge gebed, and hu cl\u00e6ne\nEala hwider ic w\u00e6s gel\u00e6d and hwanon ic eom nu gebroht.\n\u00dea het Martianus mid his hospwordum \u00fe\u00e6t he ful s\u00e6de his si\u00f0 him eallum.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00fe se geeadcucoda, me coman to silhearwan atelices hiwes swa heage swa entes, mid\nHeora earmes w\u00e6ron swylce orm\u00e6te beames, heora clawa scearpe, and hi sylfa unmildheorta.\n\u00deas \u00feyllice me tugon to \u00fe\u00e6re sweartan helle.\n\u00d0a mid \u00feam \u00fee Iulianus his drihten geb\u00e6d \u00fe\u00e6t he me eft ar\u00e6rde, \u00fea unrotsodon helware and of godes\n\u00dea coman twegen englas and me of \u00f0am deoflum genamon and me gebrohtan to life, \u00fe\u00e6t ic nu on God\n\u00dea wear\u00f0 Martianus mycclum gedrefed, and het hi ealle gebringan binnan \u00feam cwearterne eft, and het\n\u00dea wear\u00f0 se edcucode man betwux \u00feysum gefvllod binnan \u00feam cwearterne and gebad mid \u00feam\nHi wurdon \u00fea gebrohte gebundene on racenteagum ealle to \u00feam tunnum and to \u00fe\u00e6re ontendnysse.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Martianus mid mycelre angsumnysse to \u00feam halgum werum and to his agenum suna, eala\nEala \u00feu Iuliane, \u00fee awendest minne sunu swa \u00fe\u00e6t he min ne r\u00e6c\u00f0 ne eac \u00fe\u00e6re meder.\n\u00dea com seo modor mid mycelre sarnysse and ealle hyre hyredmen to \u00fe\u00e6re heofunga, and manega o\u00f0re\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6s deman sunu to his dreorigan f\u00e6der, Ne \u00feurfe ge us bem\u00e6nan ne urne si\u00fe bewepan,\nWe fara\u00f0 \u00f0urh \u00fe\u00e6t fyr unforhte \u00feurh God, and we ansunde becuma\u00f0 eft to eowrum gesih\u00feum.\n\u00deonne \u00feu me eft gesihst gesundne of \u00feam fyre, ge\u00feafa \u00fe\u00e6t min modor me gespr\u00e6can, and sume \u00fereo\nIc wene \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu ne forleosa na\u00f0or ne hi ne me.\n\u00dea wear\u00f0 seo modor on mode geblissod, and se f\u00e6der cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00fe\u00e6s cnapan willan wolde\n\u00dea het se dema his gingran \u00feis don, and eode mid his wife aweg to his huse, for \u00fean \u00fee he ne mihte\n\u00dea het se undergerefa hi ealle gebringan into \u00f0am tunnum and ontendan hi mid acuman, and mid wuda\n\u00d0a stodan \u00fea halgan hale of \u00feam fyre glitiniende swa swa gold, \u00feus herigende God, Transiuimus per\n\u00deis geaxode se dema, and \u00feyder efste mid his wife, and \u00e6fter langsumre spr\u00e6ce let \u00fea modor to \u00feam\n\u00dea geb\u00e6don \u00fea halgan binnan \u00feam cwearterne for \u00fe\u00e6t h\u00e6\u00f0ene wif, \u00fe\u00e6t se h\u00e6lend hire gemiltsode.\n\u00d0a wear\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6r eor\u00f0styrung, and eall seo stow byfode, and \u00fe\u00e6r scean mycel leoht and m\u00e6re br\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6r\n\u00dea gelyfde heo sona on \u00feone lifigendan God, and wear\u00f0 gefullod \u00e6t \u00feam fores\u00e6dan preoste, and\n\u00dea geaxode se dema \u00feis \u00feus gedon, and het hi ealle gel\u00e6dan to his la\u00f0an andweardnysse, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 to\nSe cnapa \u00feancode gode, \u00fee hi swa gebigde to his so\u00f0an geleafan, \u00fe\u00e6t heo ne losode mid him.\n\u00dea het Martianus \u00fe\u00e6t man hi gel\u00e6hte, ac hi wurdon ablende \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6t bebod begunnon.\n\u00c6fter \u00feisum het se heardheorta dema beheafdian \u00fea cempan \u00fee on Crist gelyfdan, and \u00fea seofon\nHe het \u00fea ged\u00e6ftan \u00fe\u00e6t deofles templ, and \u00fea halgan coman \u00feider on bendum, and ealle \u00fea\n\u00dea bed Iulianus gebigedum cneowum, mid his geferum, \u00feone heofonlican God, \u00fe\u00e6t he his mihte\n\u00c6fter \u00fe\u00e6re bene tob\u00e6rst seo eor\u00f0e, and \u00fe\u00e6t templ asanc mid eallum his sacerdum, and fela \u00fe\u00e6re\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Iulianus to \u00feam cwellere \u00feus, Hw\u00e6r is nu seo f\u00e6gernys \u00feines g